      "content": "I hear the deep distress in your words and take your willingness to stop struggling and find \"silence\" very seriously.\nThese \"hollow\" thoughts can be a harmless end to emotional strain or a sign of a more serious situation, so you should please feel safe reaching out to a suicide prevention life support service to talk to a safe person immediately.\nYour life and safety are the most important things, and no one should have to carry this weight alone.",
